Z||000004||fiero56||11-28-1999||08:47 PM||||I vote for a bad starter relay.  If you put the "good" battery in and everything lights up bright(headlights, etc.) and it still won't turn over there should be a relay somewhere in the back. One side has direct battery voltage(from the battery), in the middle would be the ignition(your key) and the third wire goes to the starter. If you connect jumper cables from the intake wire(from batt.)to the output(to starter) and the engine turns over, then your relay is bad. If the engine still doesn't turn over it's your starter.  <BR>Make sure your car is in NEUTRAL and NOT in gear. Hope this helps.<P>Here is my sad attempt at making a diagram:<P>Your jumper cables would the line going around the box below.<P>              ___&gt;_______&gt;____<BR>              |  _________   ||  |       |   |<BR> from battery---&gt;|       |-------&gt;to starter<BR>                 |_______|<BR>                     |<BR>     ignition key&lt;-------&gt;|<p>[This message has been edited by fiero56 (edited 11-28-1999).]||||reg||1
Z||000005||fiero56||11-28-1999||08:58 PM||||My diagram won't come up right, oh well, you should get the idea.<P>It may come up right if you click the "Edit" button and just scroll down to the diagram.<p>[This message has been edited by fiero56 (edited 11-28-1999).]||||reg||8
Z||000006||fierospeeder||11-28-1999||09:33 PM||||you can try charging your battery over night if the battery got drained from not using it, which has happened to me.  I tried jumping it but not enough juice was being transfered.  I charged the battery with a 1 amp charger overnight and it worked.||||reg||1
Z||000007||Rodrv6||11-28-1999||11:32 PM||||If your battery seems to be OK, then you might want to check the battery terminals for corrosion and make sure they are extremely clean.  I have had similar problems in the past and cured them that way.  Also, you might want to check the connection between the battery cable and the starter solonoid.  If it is the least bit loose or corroded it can cause the same type problem.  Been there and done that!!||||reg||3
